# ASTRO BOT Rescue Mission in flat play, checked by tools/astrobot_test.py.
#
# "play <level>": the level loads from the world map, Astro gets out of the controller, the
# camera follows him and holds still while he stands, the right stick turns it, he walks and
# the camera comes along. Levels by their folder (data/multi_platformer/levels), in the
# game's own order (mup_product_levels.xml). "skip <scenario>: <why>" leaves one out, saying why.

play world0_0_new_intro_1
play world0_0_new_intro_2
play cave_trap_1
play cave_canyons_half1
play rope_boss_test_01
play beanstalk
play giant_1
play sea_whale_split1
play mine_coaster_04
play water_boss_final
play cave_canyons_half2
play giant_2
play cave_trap_2
play forest_castle
play bird_boss_test_01
play sea_whale_split2
play heaven
play world3_1_Indy_cave_split1
play world3_1_Indy_cave_split2
play spider_boss_test_01
play city_funfair_remake
play cave_graveyard
play ninja_stage
play volcano
play shark_boss_01
play final_boss
play collection_room
play challenge_credits
skip play challenge_headbutt: not in the level list World 1-1's entry reaches them by (the game asserts m_levels.count)
play challenge_cannons
play challenge_caterpillar
play challenge_extreme_platform
play challenge_waterfall
play challenge_dodgeball
skip play challenge_underwater_down: not in the level list World 1-1's entry reaches them by (the game asserts m_levels.count)
play challenge_bumpers_easy
play challenge_water_shooting
play challenge_bumpers_02
play challenge_underwater_maze
skip play challenge_perspective_01: not in the level list World 1-1's entry reaches them by (the game asserts m_levels.count)
play challenge_rope_pull_02
skip play challenge_maxi_scale2: not in the level list World 1-1's entry reaches them by (the game asserts m_levels.count)
play challenge_lasers
play challenge_vertical_tree
play challenge_wave
play challenge_storm_city
play challenge_tatami
play challenge_fire_road
play challenge_machinegun
play challenge_light
play challenge_shuriken_shooting
play challenge_lava2
play challenge_boss_gorilla
play challenge_boss_octopus
play challenge_boss_bird
play challenge_boss_spider
play challenge_boss_shark
play challenge_boss_final

# "open the gadget chest in <level> at <x y z> facing <degrees>" (its place and heading in its
# level file): Astro stands in front of it with the seat behind him and punches it; it opens where
# it is (the game's chest flies to the player's head otherwise, through Astro) and he stays.
# ", then hook the ring at <x y z>": with the hook it gives, the camera turned to that ring and a
# swipe forward (R1), the rope holds on it.
open the gadget chest in beanstalk at 0.00 -4.22 -43.21 facing 0
open the gadget chest in bird_boss_test_01 at 0.00 -0.19 9.05 facing 0
open the gadget chest in cave_canyons_half1 at 0.00 0.20 15.93 facing 0
open the gadget chest in cave_canyons_half1 at 0.00 0.20 15.93 facing 0, then hook the ring at 0.00 0.81 14.75
open the gadget chest in cave_canyons_half2 at 0.88 0.18 -10.83 facing -45
open the gadget chest in cave_graveyard at -0.07 1.16 5.25 facing -13
skip open the gadget chest in challenge_boss_bird at 0.00 0.33 1.67 facing 0: a challenge starts with its gadget fitted (no chest at its start)
